      "description": "Custom sort-arrow icon: a Material Symbols ligature name (e.g. \"north\",\n\"expand_less\"). Empty = the built-in SVG arrow. The icon still rotates\n180deg for descending via the same CSS, so pick an \"ascending-pointing\"\nglyph."
    },
    {
      "name": "inactiveIcon",
      "type": "'always' | 'hover'",
      "default": "'always'",
      "defaultValue": "always",
      "options": [
        "always",
        "hover"
      ],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "inactive-icon",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "When the arrow is visible on a column that is NOT the active sort.\n\n- `always` — dimmed but present at rest (default). The arrow is the only\n  thing distinguishing a sortable column from a fixed one, so hiding it\n  until hover means the affordance cannot be discovered without hovering\n  every header — and cannot be discovered at all on a touch device, which\n  has no hover state to give.\n- `hover`  — invisible until the header is hovered or focused. Quieter in a\n  table where nearly every column sorts and the arrows become noise.\n\nThe ACTIVE column's arrow is always fully opaque under either setting."
    },
    {
